  "description": "Async pipeline runtime for .NET: resource-gated concurrency with adaptive/Bayesian tuning (and a pluggable custom-tuner hook, e.g. the always-learning EvalApp.Neural), sagas with compensation, middleware, pipelines that compose (a step can run another pipeline or itself; a context can hold pipelines, so outer loops drive inner pipelines), exclusive-resource guards that fail loudly or queue when two flows touch something non-thread-safe, and a fluent builder. One entry point, one namespace: `using EvalApp;` then `Eval.App(...)...` — the whole public surface lives directly in the EvalApp namespace — no separate \"consumer\" namespace to learn. The shared runtime for Evaluated Applications products.",
